### Team Notes API: runnable examples (VS Code REST Client / Visual Studio / Rider)
### Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/TeamNotes.Api --launch-profile http
### Seeded demo users (Development only, identity via X-User-Id; impersonation, not authentication):
###   Alice 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111  Owner of Apollo
###   Bob   22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222  Member of Apollo and Gemini
###   Carol 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333  Owner of Gemini

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@carol = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@apollo = aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@gemini = aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@welcomeNote = bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@alicePrivateNote = bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### Health (no identity needed) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### No identity -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/teams

### Bob's teams -> Apollo and Gemini, both Member
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/teams
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Bob creates a team-visible note in Apollo -> 201, Location, ETag "1"
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Sprint goals", "body": "Ship the notes API", "visibility": "Team" }

### Alice (Apollo owner) reads Bob's team note -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}{{created.response.headers.Location}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### Carol is not in Apollo -> 404 (indistinguishable from a missing note)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{created.response.headers.Location}}
X-User-Id: {{carol}}

### Bob reads Alice's PRIVATE note in his own team -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{alicePrivateNote}}
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Alice reads her own private note -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{alicePrivateNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### Right note, wrong team route -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{gemini}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Blank title -> 400 ProblemDetails naming the field
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "   ", "body": "" }

### Alice cannot post into Gemini -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{gemini}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Intrusion", "body": "" }

### ---- Editing and concurrency ----
### Run these in order; they start from the seeded welcome note at version 1.

### Bob edits the shared note with the version he read -> 200, ETag "2"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{bob}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Welcome to Apollo (edited by Bob)", "body": "Updated agenda" }

### Alice still holds version 1 -> 412, response ETag tells her the current version
PUT {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Alice's edit", "body": "" }

### No If-Match -> 428
PUT {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Blind write", "body": "" }

### Wildcard is not accepted -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Blind write", "body": "" }

### Bob can edit but not delete Alice's team note -> 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{bob}}
If-Match: "2"

### Alice (author and owner) deletes with the current version -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
If-Match: "2"

### Gone -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes/{{welcomeNote}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### ---- Listing and search ----

### Bob's view of Apollo: only the team note (Alice's private draft is filtered out, also from totalCount)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Alice's view: both notes
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### Paging
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes?page=1&pageSize=1
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### Search is literal: "%" matches a percent sign, not everything -> 0 results
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes?q=%25
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Searching for words in a note Bob cannot see finds nothing -> totalCount 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes?q=private
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### pageSize over 100 -> 400 naming pageSize (not silently clamped)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes?pageSize=500
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### Carol is not in Apollo -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{apollo}}/notes
X-User-Id: {{carol}}
